# AR-12 / E-102 (platform.r43_faults fault_id
# E102_MIGRATION_LEDGER_LINE_ENDING_HASH_SPLIT): drizzle-orm hashes migration
# files as raw bytes with no line-ending normalization, so whichever
# machine/CI runner's checkout convention (LF vs Windows CRLF, controlled by
# git's core.autocrlf) wrote a file determines the hash baked into
# drizzle.__drizzle_migrations forever. This does NOT retroactively fix the
# existing split (that would mean rewriting an already-applied migration
# file's bytes or its recorded ledger hash -- both real risks to a live
# system, not taken unilaterally here) -- it only forces every NEW
# drizzle/*.sql commit to converge on one convention (LF) regardless of which
# OS or editor authored it, so this specific class of drift cannot recur for
# any migration added from this point forward. See
# scripts/check-migration-integrity.mjs for the CI-side enforcement this
# pairs with.
drizzle/*.sql text eol=lf
